Week 3 Data Preparation Note — Kaduna North Flood Exposure

1. Coordinate Reference System (CRS)

The data was reprojected from EPSG:4326 (WGS 84) to EPSG:32632 (WGS 84 / UTM Zone 32N). This projected CRS uses metres and is suitable for spatial analysis in the Kaduna North study area.

2. Data Reprojected and Clipped

The following datasets were reprojected to EPSG:32632:

* Highways
* Waterways
* Waterbodies
* Buildings

The reprojected datasets were then clipped using the Kaduna North Boundary to limit the analysis to the study area.

The resulting analysis-ready layers are:

* Highway_KadunaNorth — 3,540 features
* Waterways_KadunaNorth — 3 features
* Waterbodies_KadunaNorth — 38 features
* Buildings_KadunaNorth — 94,254 features

3. Five Quality Checks

Check 1 — CRS

All prepared layers use EPSG:32632 (WGS 84 / UTM Zone 32N).
Result: Pass.

Check 2 — Geometry Type

* Highways: Line
* Waterways: Point
* Waterbodies: Polygon
* Buildings: MultiPolygon

Result: Geometry types were checked. The Waterways layer is represented as points and has been flagged for review rather than changed.

Check 3 — Feature Count

Feature counts were checked after clipping:

* Highways: 3,540
* Waterways: 3
* Waterbodies: 38
* Buildings: 94,254

Result: Pass — feature counts were recorded.

Check 4 — Geometry Validity

QGIS Check Validity was used on the prepared layers.

* Highways: 3,540 valid, 0 invalid
* Waterways: 3 valid, 0 invalid
* Waterbodies: 38 valid, 0 invalid
* Buildings: 94,254 valid, 0 invalid

Result: Pass — no invalid geometries were found.

Check 5 — Study Area / Clipping

The prepared layers were visually checked against the Kaduna North Boundary.

Result: Pass — all clipped features were within the Kaduna North study area.

4. Problems Found

The Waterways dataset was returned as point geometry rather than line geometry and was therefore flagged for review. No invalid geometries were found in the validity check.

5. Analysis-Ready File

The analysis-ready data is stored in:

Kaduna_Flood_Analysis.gpkg

The GeoPackage contains the prepared Kaduna North layers and is located in the project folder.
